      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When an onion is cut, cells are mechanically ruptured, releasing enzyme mixtures. These enzymes react with sulfur-containing compounds within the plant, producing volatile sulfur compounds like syn-propanethial S-oxide. This volatile gas then reacts with moisture in the eyes or mucous membranes to form irritating sulfuric acid, which causes the characteristic burning sensation. This whole process demonstrates how enzyme activity dictates the flavor and pungency of many vegetables.",
