      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While alliinase is a key enzyme in allium species, the onion's specific sulfur breakdown involves several different enzymes acting on various precursor molecules. The rapid irritation stems from the highly volatile nature of the sulfur compounds produced. Once the reaction occurs within the ruptured onion cells, the volatile gases are immediately released into the surrounding air, allowing them to move quickly via diffusion to the moist surfaces of the eyes. This immediate availability of irritant gas causes the sudden, intense stinging sensation.",
