    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Right, the diffusion aspect makes sense. I'm just trying to find a way to help the students visualize that \"invisible\" element—the way it feels like a sudden, mischievous little sting that catches you off guard before you even realize what's happening. Is there anything unique about the way these molecules interact with the tear film that explains that specific sensation of being \"pricked\"?",
