      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The sensation of being \"pricked\" is due to the sulfuric acid mist reacting with the delicate proteins and mucous of the tear film. Sulfuric acid is a strong irritant, and even low concentrations can denature surface proteins in the eye, inducing a rapid inflammatory response. This swift chemical burn, rather than a simple mechanical irritation, is what translates to that sharp, surprising stinging feeling. Essentially, the molecules are aggressively reacting with the vulnerable biological tissues upon contact.",
